RADIO: The time is 8:12 AM. Before our morning bulletin, a local reminder from the District Air Defense Command: [next=2]

Volunteer labor corps members are needed at the eastern rail yards this afternoon to clear freight. Also, strict enforcement of blackout curtains at dusk remains in effect. [next=2.5]

RADIO: Moving to regional defense... The general air-raid alert for the Kiyoshima district is now a light advisory. [next=2]

Radar reports a single high-altitude enemy plane approaching from the east. Command assesses it as a weather flight. Anti-aircraft guns will stand down and shelter is not required. [next=2.5]

RADIO: Citizens may return to work. Stay alert, but there is no immediate danger. [next=1.5]
=> END